From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:09:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] journeys viewer: the canvas laid out as its printed pages,
 each part under its module; the schedule at a glance near the top
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner (2026-11-19): the interactive canvas sheets should look exactly
like the source PDF, each part with its module (M1, M2 …), with no
additional questions; and presenters and participants should see the
schedule towards the top.

Canvas (schemas/process/workshop.ts, scripts/journeys/canvas-form.ts):
- a sheet's kicker band, header write-ins (Country, Table; same shares the
  cover's key), footer, and the canvas's masthead;
- a section's number badge, minutes, note, DISCUSS and RULES lines, the
  modules it is worked in (shown as linked chips), layout (stack, columns
  with an optional split, aside, row) and tone (box, warm, cool, gap);
- new field types: blanks (a sentence with ___ write-ins), note, table
  (printed, no answer), cards (side by side with arrows, or one per row,
  each with its own fields);
- grid columns of printed words (label), a choice or ticks per cell, and
  option columns forming one radio per row (the gap strip's urgency), with
  per-row options and heading rows (group);
- annex: false, so a sheet carries only its own fields;
- the PDF model and writer follow (printed words, heading rows, headings
  alone, write-ins among ticks), and the summary lists every key once.

Schedule (scripts/journeys/schedule.ts): scheduleGlanceHtml, a tab per day
with this track's sessions and the shared slots, one line each, now and
next marked by the device's clock; first on the overview and the
discussion, under the title on the workshop page. A module page says when
it is taught and lists its canvas parts, linked into the discussion. The
lab no longer writes its step into the address on arrival, so a plain
visit opens at the top.

